WEBVTT

00:46:58.958 --> 00:47:03.184
And I in American parlance
can be seen as someone who pulls.

00:47:03.208 --> 00:47:05.601
Because I ask, it's not just one or two,

00:47:05.625 --> 00:47:07.059
you know, I take it in,

00:47:07.083 --> 00:47:10.059
then I sit with it
and then I make it my own.

00:47:10.083 --> 00:47:13.976
But I am completely shaped
through these conversations

00:47:14.000 --> 00:47:17.226
rather than sitting with myself,
thinking it through, trying it out,

00:47:17.250 --> 00:47:19.559
and it's a completely different model.

00:47:19.583 --> 00:47:21.601
AG: So I feel very clear

00:47:21.625 --> 00:47:23.893
that I've learned something
from this discussion

00:47:23.917 --> 00:47:25.684
because when you asked the question,

00:47:25.708 --> 00:47:29.601
OK, were you raised
to be autonomous or to be loyal,

00:47:29.625 --> 00:47:31.018
my first impulse was to say,